amneziawg-linux-kmod (1.0.20260929+awg-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Transport packets with the length of a handshake message are no longer
    dropped as bad handshakes (up to 75% loss at one packet size for some
    S values).
  * Handshakes from unknown peers are no longer reported over netlink by
    default (unknown_peer_notify module parameter); where supported only
    admins can listen.
  * Kernel limits Jc <= 128 and Jmin/Jmax <= 1280. Jmin = Jmax is kept.
  * AWG parameters are swapped atomically (RCU); I1-I5 are prepared before
    a configuration is applied; stricter I1-I5 syntax.
  * DKMS no longer rebuilds the initramfs.

 -- Advanced-WG <237044+V-Bantserov@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 05:48:00 +0300

amneziawg-linux-kmod (1.0.20260928+awg-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Builds on current RHEL/AlmaLinux 8.10 and 9.8 and CentOS Stream 10:
    backported kernel APIs are detected from the headers instead of the
    kernel version.
  * Builds on kernels older than 5.10 (zinc crypto) and Ubuntu 18.04.
  * tests/compile-matrix.sh: 18 distribution kernels, 4.15 to 7.2.

 -- Advanced-WG <237044+V-Bantserov@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:30:00 +0300

amneziawg-linux-kmod (1.0.20260927+awg-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release of the patched fork (AmneziaWG 2.0 protocol), based on
    upstream 26f5df0. Changes in docs/CHANGELOG.md, among them:
  * AWG parameters are validated as a whole before anything is applied; a
    rejected "awg set" no longer leaves invalid values active (crashes of
    upstream #254 / #225) or a changed listen port.
  * Plain WireGuard, AWG 1.0 and AWG 2.0 peers without S3/S4 on one
    obfuscated interface, detected per peer and reported over netlink.
  * A replayed old handshake initiation can no longer switch a peer to
    unobfuscated framing.
  * I1-I5 size overflow, use-after-free on teardown, netlink dump with
    many peers and other upstream bugs fixed.
  * Builds on Linux 7.1/7.2, distro kernels with the new udp_tunnel API,
    RHEL/AlmaLinux 10.2-10.3; the zinc assembly files needed before 5.10
    are back.
  * Packaging: correct DKMS version in dkms.conf, debhelper compat 13.

 -- Advanced-WG <237044+V-Bantserov@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0300

